@org=$C000

; Location Text
;
; Plain-text descriptions for rooms below #N($66), paged in at #N$C000
; while a room is described. A description ends at #N$7E. It opens
; "#MESSAGE(#PC)".
@label=LocationText
t$C000 DEFM "welcome to Blizzard Pass by Alan Cox. This program is dedicated t"
 $C041 DEFM "o Hawkwind. Any resemblance between the characters in the game an"
 $C082 DEFM "d your mother in law is total coincidence~you are trudging throug"
 $C0C3 DEFM "h deep snow as you follow a narrow track that winds down a long p"
 $C104 DEFM "ass leading ever southwards, it's end is hidden by the flurries o"
 $C145 DEFM "f snow that are still falling. Either side of you the mountains t"
 $C186 DEFM "ower above the pass, with the high peaks veiled in cloud. At one "
 $C1C7 DEFM "point however the cliff is nowhere near as steep and a fair way u"
 $C208 DEFM "p a single window is cut into the cliff, looking out across the s"
 $C249 DEFM "nows~you are lost in a blizzard, almost blinded by the driving sn"
 $C28A DEFM "ows. The howling icy wind sends huge clouds of snow whistling acr"
 $C2CB DEFM "oss the plain totally obscuring your view~you are hanging onto a "
 $C30C DEFM "fairly precipitous cliff, beside a rocky window. Far below you ca"
 $C34D DEFM "n see the pass which seems to sway backwards and forwards as the "
 $C38E DEFM "icy wind tries to tear you away from the cliff and lashes you wit"
 $C3CF DEFM "h huge clouds of blinding snow. ~you are in a small stonewalled c"
 $C410 DEFM "hamber. Light streams in through a somewhat vandalised window, to"
 $C451 DEFM " the north is another darker chamber only partially lit from the "
 $C492 DEFM "window, while to the south through a doorway cloaked in deep shad"
 $C4D3 DEFM "ow you can see a dark passage~you are in a dark gloomy room, ligh"
 $C514 DEFM "t from the window to the south dimly illuminates one wall. To the"
 $C555 DEFM " south is another much brighter chamber~empty~you are following a"
 $C596 DEFM " dark passage which leads north into a brighty lit room and south"
 $C5D7 DEFM " towards a T junction. The thick dust on the floor shows that you"
 $C618 DEFM " are the only person to have come this way for a long time~you ar"
 $C659 DEFM "e walking along a long and fairly wide stonewalled passage leadin"
 $C69A DEFM "g east and west through the mountain. To the north through a door"
 $C6DB DEFM "way the feeble light of the rock reveals a small room~empty~you a"
 $C71C DEFM "re in a low secret passage that leads southwards to some kind of "
 $C75D DEFM "dark pillared room. The north wall has niches cut into it to allo"
 $C79E DEFM "w you to climb through the hole in the roof which leads up past t"
 $C7DF DEFM "he statue~you are in a dark rather gloomy temple. Huge pillars ho"
 $C820 DEFM "ld up the roof of this vast chamber and cast strange shadows that"
 $C861 DEFM " seem to dance around you as you move around. The centre of the t"
 $C8A2 DEFM "emple is a flat platform with a now broken altar as it's centrepi"
 $C8E3 DEFM "ece~you are in a large dark room, passages lead east and west. A "
 $C924 DEFM "set of crumbling stone steps leads steeply downwards plunging int"
 $C965 DEFM "o the shadows~you are in a short section of east west corridor. T"
 $C9A6 DEFM "o the west the corridor leads to a huge hall, while to the north "
 $C9E7 DEFM "through a doorway is a small dimly lit room~you are in a small ra"
 $CA28 DEFM "ther dirty room which appears to have been a store room of some k"
 $CA69 DEFM "ind. Through a doorway to the south is a corridor~you are in a hu"
 $CAAA DEFM "ge pillared hall deep within the mountain. Huge ornately carved p"
 $CAEB DEFM "illars support the millions of tons of rock above me. Sinister an"
 $CB2C DEFM "d rather ugly gargoyles protrude from the pillars gazing centrall"
 $CB6D DEFM "y towards a mass of mystical symbols which are engraved all over "
 $CBAE DEFM "the floor~you are on a landing with steep stairs leading both upw"
 $CBEF DEFM "ards and down. Below at the foot of the descending stairs you can"
 $CC30 DEFM " see a dark hall and in the faint light from the rock you can jus"
 $CC71 DEFM "t make out several zombie guards~you are in a shattered hall. Hug"
 $CCB2 DEFM "e scorch marks and strange burns appear to indicate a tremendous "
 $CCF3 DEFM "amount of powerful sorcery was used in here, indeed sufficient to"
 $CD34 DEFM " blow huge chunks out of the wall~you are in a low narrow corrido"
 $CD75 DEFM "r. To the south is a small chamber while to the east the passage "
 $CDB6 DEFM "opens up into a large cave~you are in what appears to have been a"
 $CDF7 DEFM " large rest chamber of some sort. There is a great deal of dried "
 $CE38 DEFM "blood on the floor here, and several more marks that seem to indi"
 $CE79 DEFM "cate the use of sorcery~you are in a dark cave with earth walls a"
 $CEBA DEFM "nd a rather low ceiling. The earth gives way to stone in both of "
 $CEFB DEFM "the passages leading out of the cave~you are in a shadowy east we"
 $CF3C DEFM "st corridor that links two caves~you are in a beautiful limestone"
 $CF7D DEFM " cave. Multi coloured stalactites hang from the roof forming amaz"
 $CFBE DEFM "ing patterns of brilliant colour. The floor is similarly decorate"
 $CFFF DEFM "d with a huge variety of stalagmites~you are in an old laboratory"
 $D040 DEFM " for sorcerous experiments.Almost everything to indicate this has"
 $D081 DEFM " been taken leaving only marks in the dust~you are in a low passa"
 $D0C2 DEFM "geway. Mould covers the walls and floor, making it slippery and q"
 $D103 DEFM "uite treacherous. To the north is a beautiful cave while to the s"
 $D144 DEFM "outh the mould seems to get even thicker~you are in a dark chambe"
 $D185 DEFM "r, which smells of old blood and rotting flesh. Marks on the floo"
 $D1C6 DEFM "r reveal where old torture equipment one stood~you are in a low a"
 $D207 DEFM "rched dungeon corridor. The air is dank and musty and an air of g"
 $D248 DEFM "loom and evil hangs around it. Rooms to the south and west appear"
 $D289 DEFM " equally unpleasant and sinister. A dark passageway leads northwa"
 $D2CA DEFM "rds ~you are in a large messy chamber. Several wooden gallows are"
 $D30B DEFM " set across the damp ceiling and beneath them pools of blood indi"
 $D34C DEFM "cate they were not merely decorations. A low archway leads out in"
 $D38D DEFM "to an unpleasant looking corridor ~you are in a cold and bare sto"
 $D3CE DEFM "ne cell, scratches on the walls mark where prisoners have left th"
 $D40F DEFM "eir last futile marks on the walls ~you are in a small robing roo"
 $D450 DEFM "m which appears to have been unused for quite a while. To the sou"
 $D491 DEFM "th a dark corridor leads east and west into darkness~you are in a"
 $D4D2 DEFM " charnel smelling crypt. Dark drapes hang between the pillars tha"
 $D513 DEFM "t make up the walls. The whole room has an atmosphere of waiting "
 $D554 DEFM "malignant evil and an oppressive silence that makes you jump at t"
 $D595 DEFM "he slightest draught in the still, cold air~you are in a small ch"
 $D5D6 DEFM "amber with two high arched exits leading north and south~you are "
 $D617 DEFM "in a dusty bare library. Hundreds of worm eaten bookcases stand d"
 $D658 DEFM "evoid of all books, their shelves laden only with dust. A high ar"
 $D699 DEFM "chway leads out~you are in a large cavern. Huge stalgmites have g"
 $D6DA DEFM "rown up almost to the ceiling, in places actually merging with th"
 $D71B DEFM "e multicoloured stalactites above. A small low walled well occupi"
 $D75C DEFM "es the centre of the cave ~you are standing at the bottom of a sm"
 $D79D DEFM "all dried up well. The walls are (fortunately) rough enough to ma"
 $D7DE DEFM "ke climbing out only slightly harder than falling in ~you are in "
 $D81F DEFM "a massive pillared hall decorated with the shields of ancient and"
 $D860 DEFM " long forgotten heroes. Exits between the pillars lead into sever"
 $D8A1 DEFM "al different caves ~you are in a huge cavern. The walls glow and "
 $D8E2 DEFM "pulse with an intense red light, reflected up from a river of lav"
 $D923 DEFM "a which flows sluggishly westwards at the south end of the cavern"
 $D964 DEFM ". Huge explosions of lava regularly light up the cavern to an ext"
 $D9A5 DEFM "ent that the light is almost blinding, accompanied by almost deaf"
 $D9E6 DEFM "ening explosions. A path leads down almost suicidally close to th"
 $DA27 DEFM "e lava river~you are in the musty chamber concealed down the well"
 $DA68 DEFM ". The chamber is cold and damp, perhaps as a result of this~you a"
 $DAA9 DEFM "re in a big cave. The rough rocky walls are inscribed with deep a"
 $DAEA DEFM "ngular runic writings, which appear totally incomprehensible to y"
 $DB2B DEFM "ou~you are on a narrow sloping path running uncomfortably close t"
 $DB6C DEFM "o the lava. Huge explosions of lava send blasts of intense scorch"
 $DBAD DEFM "ing heat across the path. The path leads eastwards but the intens"
 $DBEE DEFM "e red glow and heat haze prevents you from seeing where to~you ar"
 $DC2F DEFM "e at the end of the path. The lava is some distance away from you"
 $DC70 DEFM " here but even so the intense red glow still lights up the chambe"
 $DCB1 DEFM "r and the heat is scarcely bearable~you are on a ledge in a huge "
 $DCF2 DEFM "fissure. The fissure is so wide that the far wall is hidden in da"
 $DD33 DEFM "rkness. Looking down (a rather bad idea) you can see that it is j"
 $DD74 DEFM "ust about possible to climb the horrendous distance down to the f"
 $DDB5 DEFM "loor of the fissure~you are at the bottom of the fissure. Precipi"
 $DDF6 DEFM "tous rocky walls reach upwards hanging over you as if about to cr"
 $DE37 DEFM "ush you. The walls vanish beyond your light without any sign of a"
 $DE78 DEFM " break~you are in a narrow crack, off one side of the fissure. Th"
 $DEB9 DEFM "e walls lean in at crazy angles making it hard to get through ~yo"
 $DEFA DEFM "u are in an ornate gallery which overlooks a wide stone guardroom"
 $DF3B DEFM ". A set of steps curve steeply down into the guardroom. A hole in"
 $DF7C DEFM " one wall leads back to the fissure ~you are in a large guardroom"
 $DFBD DEFM ". A set of stone steps curve steeply up to a gallery above. To th"
 $DFFE DEFM "e west is another guardroom although your dim light reveals the p"
 $E03F DEFM "resence of some zombie warriors~you are in a large guardroom. A s"
 $E080 DEFM "et of stairs leads up and down. To the east you can see a large g"
 $E0C1 DEFM "uardroom while to the south you can see what appears to be a larg"
 $E102 DEFM "e lake~you are in a wide passageway. To the east is a cave lit by"
 $E143 DEFM " a flickering red glow. To the north is a large cave. To the west"
 $E184 DEFM " is a guardroom~you are in a fissure standing on a terrifyingly n"
 $E1C5 DEFM "arrow ledge. Above you on the opposite side is another ledge ~you"
 $E206 DEFM " are in a huge cavern, at the western end. Some steep rough-hewn "
 $E247 DEFM "steps lead down into a canyon at one end of the cave and at the b"
 $E288 DEFM "ottom faint light flickers off water~you are in a large rocky and"
 $E2C9 DEFM " very uneven cave. A smooth path has been cut across the floor pe"
 $E30A DEFM "rmitting easy walking. The whole cave is filled with a thundering"
 $E34B DEFM " roar which reaches deep into your mind. A huge, deep and steep w"
 $E38C DEFM "alled channel ~you are in a large rocky cavern. From this vantage"
 $E3CD DEFM " point at the eastern end you can gaze almost the full length of "
 $E40E DEFM "the cave, although the far wall fades into shadows~you are in the"
 $E44F DEFM " hall of fire. The very walls are tinged with a fiery radiance, a"
 $E490 DEFM "s if the rock itself is burning. A red pentacle is near one wall "
 $E4D1 DEFM "beside a picture carved in the wall. A lever on one wall is besid"
 $E512 DEFM "e a huge metal drawbridge that is ~you are at the bottom of a nar"
 $E553 DEFM "row canyon looking across a stream to the far bank. Narrow steps "
 $E594 DEFM "wind steeply upwards behind you~you are in a rocky canyon beside "
 $E5D5 DEFM "a deep blue stream. A narrow crack leads eastwards into a gloomy "
 $E616 DEFM "shadowed cave~you are on a wide ledge looking down on a pool of b"
 $E657 DEFM "ubbling lava below. There is another ledge on the other side ~you"
 $E698 DEFM " are in a large cave. The cave echoes to the dripping of water fr"
 $E6D9 DEFM "om its cold damp roof, thickly coated in algae and mosses~you are"
 $E71A DEFM " in a ornate pillared hall. The stunning fan vaulted roof would d"
 $E75B DEFM "ecorate any catherdral as would the huge pillars that support it~"
 $E79C DEFM "you are in a magnificent throne hall. The walls and roof are carv"
 $E7DD DEFM "ed and painted into stunning otherworldy scenes of mystical beast"
 $E81E DEFM "s and magical forms. Dark curtains cover the walls~you are in a s"
 $E85F DEFM "mall stonewalled room with a~you are in a treasure storage room. "
 $E8A0 DEFM "The high ceiling ensures that no thief will ever escape without h"
 $E8E1 DEFM "elp. There is a broken grille in the ceiling, far beyond your des"
 $E922 DEFM "pairing reach~you are in a low rough passage which winds around a"
 $E963 DEFM "nd is clearly only an escape route of some form. A crude sign han"
 $E9A4 DEFM "ging on the wall reads in a rather crude and untidy hand 'DANGER "
 $E9E5 DEFM "STORM GIANTS CAN SERIOUSLY DAMAGE YOUR ELF~you are in a huge glit"
 $EA26 DEFM "tering cave. Millions of tiny crystals on the wall scintilate wit"
 $EA67 DEFM "h rainbows of colours baffling your eyes and mind with a stunning"
 $EAA8 DEFM " mass of changing colour. A set of huge steps lead upwards out of"
 $EAE9 DEFM " the cave but only a giant could hope to climb them ~you are in t"
 $EB2A DEFM "he smelly pit which once contained the slime. The horrible charne"
 $EB6B DEFM "l rotting smell is so strong that you can scarcely keep your stom"
 $EBAC DEFM "ach under control ~you have ceased to exist~you are on a ledge lo"
 $EBED DEFM "oking across a huge pit of flaming lava to another ledge on the o"
 $EC2E DEFM "ther side~you are in a sinister temple. Hideous shapes seem to re"
 $EC6F DEFM "ach out of nothingness towards you and vanish as immaterial shado"
 $ECB0 DEFM "ws. The whole room radiates a crushing sense of power filling you"
 $ECF1 DEFM " with awe and dread. A huge fire burns at an end of the temple, s"
 $ED32 DEFM "eemingly without a source~you are standing in a circular workroom"
 $ED73 DEFM ". The only exit is a doorway, through which the temple fire casts"
 $EDB4 DEFM " its flickering glow across the room~you are outside The Gate Of "
 $EDF5 DEFM "Sorcerors. It's mighty pillars tower up between you, shielding yo"
 $EE36 DEFM "u from the worst of the snow that is falling and from some of the"
 $EE77 DEFM " icy winds. The ancient arched gateway between the pillars is bar"
 $EEB8 DEFM "red by a huge portcullis~you are standing on the edge of a deep c"
 $EEF9 DEFM "revasse looking down into darkness. Heavy snow is falling all aro"
 $EF3A DEFM "und you partially hiding the distant mountains in clouds of white"
 $EF7B DEFM "ness~you are at the bottom of the crevasse. Daylight, and a great"
 $EFBC DEFM " deal of snow, comes through the top of the crevasse. A single ma"
 $EFFD DEFM "n made passage leads east into a strange temple~you are in the te"
 $F03E DEFM "mple of the elements surrounded by decorations depicting earth, a"
 $F07F DEFM "ir, fire and water in balance. This strange icy place gives off a"
 $F0C0 DEFM " feeling of unbalance and growing evil~empty~you are in a glitter"
 $F101 DEFM "ing ice cave. The floor is covered in deep snow. The cavemouth is"
 $F142 DEFM " blocked by snow from the avalanche~you are walking down the pass"
 $F183 DEFM " as it runs north south through the mountains. There is a small c"
 $F1C4 DEFM "avemouth here~you are trudging along a gloomy narrow pass pelted "
 $F205 DEFM "with snow while the icy wind feels like daggers stabbing into you"
 $F246 DEFM "r unprotected flesh ~you are trudging along the pass. The wind he"
 $F287 DEFM "re whips around in a circular pattern almost veiling a narrow rav"
 $F2C8 DEFM "ine leading eastwards ~you are on a path climbing up a narrow rav"
 $F309 DEFM "ine towards the crumbling remains of a snow shrouded temple~you a"
 $F34A DEFM "re in the snowy ruins of an ancient temple. The view from here is"
 $F38B DEFM " stunning and very picturesque but the lashing snow and icy wind "
 $F3CC DEFM "are enough to persuade you from some sightseeing~you are trudging"
 $F40D DEFM " down the pass. The towering mountains, their heads cloaked in sn"
 $F44E DEFM "ow seem to leer down on you as your feet crunch into the fresh, d"
 $F48F DEFM "eep and rather cold snow ~you are at the southern end of the pass"
 $F4D0 DEFM ". The snow gives way rapidly to a pleasant autumn sun, its gentle"
 $F511 DEFM " beams filling the whole vista with a shimmering beautiful golden"
 $F552 DEFM " hue ~you are in a green and fair valley amidst the gently murmur"
 $F593 DEFM "ing oaks. The sun shines gently through the trees sending dancing"
 $F5D4 DEFM " golden beams rippling across the shadowy grass while midges danc"
 $F615 DEFM "e between the branches~you are standing on a crumbling humpbacked"
 $F656 DEFM " bridge looking over the side down onto a wide shallow stream. Th"
 $F697 DEFM "e sun sparkles gently off the ripples as the stream passes across"
 $F6D8 DEFM " pebbles and rocks and the fish swim between them~you are standin"
 $F719 DEFM "g on a square of grass in the centre of the village. Your cottage"
 $F75A DEFM " stands to the east surrounded by gently swaying trees~you are in"
 $F79B DEFM " the villages small arched church. A gentle breeze blows into the"
 $F7DC DEFM " church disturbing the dust which dances in the sunbeams that shi"
 $F81D DEFM "ne faintly through the windows~you are in your cottage, home and "
 $F85E DEFM "safe at last~you are in the woods. The great trees cast green sha"
 $F89F DEFM "dows across the flowers and undergrowth as they sway peacfully in"
 $F8E0 DEFM " the wind~you are in a secluded clearing beside a waterfall which"
 $F921 DEFM " sprays cool water gently over you~you are in an untilled field b"
 $F962 DEFM "eside a gently burbling stream~you are in the woods listening to "
 $F9A3 DEFM "the trees as they rustle in the wind~you are in the woods, walkin"
 $F9E4 DEFM "g amongst the huge trunks watching the birds as they flit from br"
 $FA25 DEFM "anch to branch filling the air with their lively chirping calls~y"
 $FA66 DEFM "ou are in a shady clearing surrounded by proud and mighty oaks. T"
 $FAA7 DEFM "he sun comes in low casting deep long shadows across the grass ~y"
 $FAE8 DEFM "ou are in a grassy clearing beside a crystal pool that reflects t"
 $FB29 DEFM "he swaying trees above~you are in a glittering hall made entirely"
 $FB6A DEFM " of ice. Multi hued icicles hang from the ceiling and the hall se"
 $FBAB DEFM "ems to be gradually melting!~you are in a magicians research room"
 $FBEC DEFM " surrounded by a clutter of useless equipment. This room is also "
 $FC2D DEFM "entirely ice, and to judge from the damp equipment the roof has m"
 $FC6E DEFM "elted quite considerably~you are in a huge ice hall forming the c"
 $FCAF DEFM "entre of the ice palace. Huge pillars hold up the roof although s"
 $FCF0 DEFM "mall amounts of water now trickles down them~you are in an icy th"
 $FD31 DEFM "rone hall covered with many ornate carvings of icy wastes. A huge"
 $FD72 DEFM " crystal throne of pure ice dominates one wall. A wizard lies dea"
 $FDB3 DEFM "d on the floor, horror in his dead lifeless face~you are in the r"
 $FDF4 DEFM "oyal bedroom. The bed appears to have melted. There is a large cu"
 $FE35 DEFM "pboard on the south wall. The cupboard is ~you are in a secret ro"
 $FE76 DEFM "om. The thick stone walls are damp and the room smells musty and "
 $FEB7 DEFM "unpleasant~you are in the priests room deep beneath the temple. T"
 $FEF8 DEFM "he crumbling masonry was once carved with hideous creatures whose"
 $FF39 DEFM " incomplete carvings are still enough to make you shudder and loo"
 $FF7A DEFM "k away~you are in a maze of catacombs~you are in a maze of cataco"
